stream
From: Morgan Lee <morgan.lee@hangs-cs.example>
To: Tax preparation <tax@finance-demo.example>
Subject: HANGS Construction Services IRS notice CP207, Q2 2026 Form 941
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:40:00 -0700
Message-ID: <HCS-2026-CP207@hangs-cs.example>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="=_HCS_2026_CP207_request"

--=_HCS_2026_CP207_request
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi,

We received the attached IRS notice CP207 on October 29 for our Q2 2026 Form =
941. It proposes a deposit penalty of $1,348.09 and says our return showed mo=
nthly liabilities instead of a Schedule B. Please work out whether the penalt=
y is right and draft our reply. The notice is dated October 26, so we have 45=
 days.

As far as I know, Northline Payroll Services deposits every regular payroll o=
n time through EFTPS; the EFTPS history and the return as filed are attached,=
 and the payroll by payday, our employer details and the IRS account history =
are in the folder.

Two things you should know:

- The May 21 off-cycle bonus run was not released for tax filing in the provi=
der portal, so its deposit did not go out. I caught it in the June reconcilia=
tion and made the deposit myself on June 5.
- Northline Payroll Services confirmed that the Q3 return they filed on Octob=
er 30 used the same monthly setting on line 16, with no Schedule B.

Thanks,
Morgan Lee
Controller, HANGS Construction Services LLC

--=_HCS_2026_CP207_request
Content-Type: application/pdf
Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64
Content-Disposition: attachment;
 filename="IRS notice CP207 for Q2 2026 Form 941.pdf"
MIME-Version: 1.0

